A better example might be if you have a wide variety of potions. You 
might have 20 or so of the proper potions, including healing, speed, 
extra healing, full healing, gain level, and gain energy. They may be of 
various buc-status. By proper dipping, you could probably manage to 
convert those 20 potions into about 15 uncursed diluted potions of full 
healing, which can then be blessed and drank for 120 more hp.

Consider that 20 potions is really a pretty low estimate for a character 
in the midgame who's been collecting them, you can end up with a lot of 
hp pretty quickly. Polypiling can create even more of the proper 
potions. Also, you can turn full healing potions into potions of gain 
ability, to fill out any missing stat points, or you may even want to 
use alchemy to create smoky potions in hopes of a wish.

Really, just try mixing some stacks. Your goal is probably potions of 
full healing or gain ability, which can be blessed for great effect. 
Gain energy/level can be useful too, but the ingredients are more rare. 
You'll quickly realize how useful this is.

